==============================================================================
 SECTION 12B : LEAKAGE CHECK - FORWARD-LOOKING PREDICTION
==============================================================================
The near-perfect scores above are expected and must NOT be read as
genuine predictive skill. The HighValue label was DERIVED from K-Means
on the same behavioural features, so the classifiers are essentially
re-learning a cluster boundary that is already a function of the inputs.
This is target leakage by construction.

A fair test asks a genuinely predictive question:
  'Using only the FIRST part of the year, can we predict who will end
   the year in the high-value segment?'

Observation window : 2010-12-01 23:27:00 -> 2011-07-13 11:54:36 
Outcome window     : 2011-07-13 11:54:36 -> 2011-12-09 12:13:00 

Customers active in the observation window: 3727 
Of these, high-value by year end          : 708 (19.0%) 

Train: 2610 | Test: 1117 

